          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "joqgfqm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Periodic Trends"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7bkzkry",
      "content": "• Atomic size decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6wwd4u2",
      "content": "• Atomic size increases down a group."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vq5rb0x",
      "content": "• Metallic character decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fwltir4",
      "content": "• Electronegativity increases across a period."
    },
    {
      "id": "7lo1k3f",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Importance of Periodic Table"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dnlumir",
      "content": "• Helps understand properties of elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Mendeleev's predicted elements: Eka-Boron (Scandium), Eka-Aluminium (Gallium), and Eka-Silicon (Germanium) are frequently asked in exams.",
        "Fluorine is the most electronegative element in the periodic table.",
        "Group 18 elements are called Noble/Inert gases and have completely filled valence shells.",
        "Hydrogen shows dual nature, resembling both Group 1 (Alkali Metals) and Group 17 (Halogens)."
      ],
      "id": "8glnsw5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "skfm0gg",
      "content": "• Predicts properties of undiscovered elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "74xkhgl",
      "content": "• Helps classify elements into groups."
    },
    {
      "id": "i8egkp5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4k5rvf4",
      "content": "• Mendeleev is called the Father of Periodic Table."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "znsqmx1",
      "content": "• Modern periodic table is based on atomic number."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "92equff",
      "content": "• There are 7 periods and 18 groups."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xey6ujt",
      "content": "• Noble gases belong to group 18."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
